<https://api.cloud.ai4eosc.eu/v1/catalog/modules/dogs-breed-detector/metadata> a it6:MachineLearningModel ;
    it6:hasMachineLearningLibrary <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/library/Keras>,
        <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/library/TensorFlow> ;
    it6:hasRepository <https://github.com/ai4os-hub/dogs-breed-detector>,
        <https://hub.docker.com/r/ai4oshub/dogs-breed-detector> ;
    it6:hasTaskType <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/tasktype/Classification>,
        <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/tasktype/Computer_Vision> ;
    it6:shortDescription "Identify a dogs breed on the image (133 known breeds)"@en ;
    it6:trainedOn <https://s3-us-west-1.amazonaws.com/udacity-aind/dog-project/dogImages.zip> ;
    dcterms:created "2024-02-25"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:description """The application applies Transfer learning for dog's breed identification, which is implemented by the means of Tensorflow and Keras. This is a modified fork of [udacity/dogs-project](https://github.com/udacity/dog-project)

From a pre-trained CNN model (VGG16 | VGG19 | Resnet50 | InceptionV3 [1]) the last layer is removed, then new Fully Connected (FC) layers are added, which are trained on the dog's dataset.

The original dataset ([2]) consists of 8351 dog's images for 133 breeds divided into: 
* training set (6680 pictures)
* validation set (835)
* test set (836)

and amounts for **1080 MB** in zipped format (see the dataset link).

**N.B.:** pre-trained weights can be found <a href=https://share.services.ai4os.eu/index.php/s/PwbSH4g4obrpbAn>here</a>

**References**
1. CNN articles: 
  * VGG: Simonyan, K., Zisserman, A.: Very deep convolutional networks for large-scale image recognition. CoRR abs/1409.1556 (2014); http://arxiv.org/abs/1409.1556
  * Resnet: He, Kaiming, Xiangyu Zhang, Shaoqing Ren, and Jian Sun: Deep residual learning for image recognition. In Proceedings of the IEEE conference on computer vision and pattern recognition, pp. 770-778. 2016. https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.03385
  * InceptionV3: Christian Szegedy, Vincent Vanhoucke, Sergey Ioffe, Jon Shlens, Zbigniew Wojna; The IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2016, pp. 2818-2826. https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.00567
2. Dogs dataset: <a href=https://s3-us-west-1.amazonaws.com/udacity-aind/dog-project/dogImages.zip> https://s3-us-west-1.amazonaws.com/udacity-aind/dog-project/dogImages.zip</a>"""@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "dogs-breed-detector" ;
    dcterms:license <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/licence/MIT> ;
    dcterms:modified "2025-03-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:title "Dogs breed detector"@en ;
    dcterms:type <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/category/AI4_inference>,
        <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/category/AI4_pre_trained> ;
    dcat:keyword "deep learning"@en,
        "image classification"@en .

<https://api.cloud.ai4eosc.eu/v1/catalog/modules/eyeonwater-yolo/metadata> a it6:MachineLearningModel ;
    it6:hasMachineLearningLibrary <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/library/TensorFlow> ;
    it6:hasRepository <https://github.com/ai4os-hub/eyeonwater-yolo>,
        <https://hub.docker.com/r/ai4oshub/eyeonwater-yolo> ;
    it6:hasTaskType <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/tasktype/Classification>,
        <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/tasktype/Computer_Vision> ;
    it6:shortDescription "Deep learning application for automated water quality assessment using YOLO algorithms."@en ;
    it6:trainedOn <https://zenodo.org/records/14017143> ;
    dcterms:created "2025-03-25"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:description """EyeOnWater YOLO is a deep learning application for water quality assessment using YOLO (You Only Look Once) object classification algorithms, integrated with the DEEPaaS API framework for scientific applications.

Water color is one of the most apparent optical characteristics observable to the human eye and serves as a primary indicator of water quality. This helps researchers classify rivers, lakes, coastal waters, seas, and oceans by colour. It can be used for both fresh and saline natural waters.

The system implements a YOLOv8-based architecture specifically adapted for water quality classification tasks. The model utilizes transfer learning from pre-trained computer vision models, fine-tuned on water quality datasets to optimize performance for aquatic environment analysis.

Key features include:
- Real-time water quality classification using convolutional neural networks
- RESTful API integration via DEEPaaS framework for scientific workflows
- Support for multi-spectral image-based water analysis
- Docker containerization for reproducible deployments

The model can classify water into different quality categories based on:
- Dissolved organic matter content: Assessment of chromophoric dissolved organic compounds
- Overall water transparency: Composite measure of water clarity and optical properties

This module provides researchers and environmental monitoring agencies with an automated tool for continuous water quality assessment, supporting ecosystem health monitoring, eutrophication detection, water treatment optimization, and regulatory compliance applications."""@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "eyeonwater-yolo" ;
    dcterms:license <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/licence/MIT> ;
    dcterms:modified "2025-07-04"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:title "EyeOnWater YOLO"@en ;
    dcterms:type <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/category/AI4_inference>,
        <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/category/AI4_pre_trained> ;
    dcat:keyword "YOLO"@en,
        "computer vision"@en,
        "deep learning"@en,
        "environmental monitoring"@en,
        "vo.imagine-ai.eu"@en,
        "water quality"@en .

<https://api.cloud.ai4eosc.eu/v1/catalog/modules/fast-neural-transfer/metadata> a it6:MachineLearningModel ;
    it6:hasMachineLearningLibrary <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/library/PyTorch> ;
    it6:hasRepository <https://github.com/ai4os-hub/fast-neural-transfer>,
        <https://hub.docker.com/r/ai4oshub/fast-neural-transfer> ;
    it6:hasTaskType <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/tasktype/Computer_Vision> ;
    it6:shortDescription "A module to apply artistic style transfer using Pytorch."@en ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:description """This is neural_transfer application using DEEPaaS API.

The module allows you to take the content of an image and reproduce it with a new artistic style using the style of a different image.

The code is based on the [Faster Neural Style Pytorch](https://github.com/pytorch/examples/tree/master/fast_neural_style) example that implements 
the method described in _Perceptual Losses for Real-Time Style Transfer and Super-Resolution_ developed by Justin Johnson, Alexandre Alahia and Li Fei-Fei [1].

**References**
1. Justin Johnson, Alexandre Alahi, Li Fei-Fei, Perceptual Losses for Real-Time Style Transfer and Super-Resolution, <a href=https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.08155>arXiv:1603.08155 [cs.CV]</a>"""@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "fast-neural-transfer" ;
    dcterms:license <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/licence/MIT> ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-11-29"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:title "Artistic Style Transfer"@en ;
    dcterms:type <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/category/AI4_inference>,
        <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/category/AI4_pre_trained> ;
    dcat:keyword "deep learning"@en,
        "image style transfer"@en .

<https://api.cloud.ai4eosc.eu/v1/catalog/modules/image-classification-tf-dicom/metadata> a it6:MachineLearningModel ;
    it6:hasMachineLearningLibrary <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/library/TensorFlow> ;
    it6:hasRepository <https://github.com/ai4os-hub/image-classification-tf-dicom>,
        <https://hub.docker.com/r/image-classification-tf-dicom> ;
    it6:hasTaskType <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/tasktype/Classification>,
        <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/tasktype/Computer_Vision> ;
    it6:shortDescription "Classify chest x-ray images in patological and non patological with this X-ray classifier."@en ;
    dcterms:created "2025-07-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:description """The deep learning revolution has brought significant advances in a number  of fields [1], primarily linked to image and speech recognition. The standardization of image classification tasks like the [ImageNet Large Scale Visual Recognition Challenge](http://www.image-net.org/challenges/LSVRC/) [2] has resulted in a reliable way to compare top performing architectures.

This Docker container contains the tools to train an image classifier on your personal dataset.

It is a highly customizable tool  that let's you choose between tens of different [top performing architectures](https://github.com/keras-team/keras-applications) and training  parameters.

The container also comes with a pretrained general-purpose image classifier trained on ImageNet.

The PREDICT method expects an RGB image as input (or the url of an RGB image) and will return a JSON with  the top 5 predictions.

<img class='fit', src='https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ai4os-hub/image-classification-tf-dicom/main/reports/figures/imagenet.png'/>

**References**

1. Yann LeCun, Yoshua Bengio, and Geofrey Hinton. [Deep learning](https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~hinton/absps/NatureDeepReview.pdf). Nature, 521(7553):436-444, May 2015.
2. Olga Russakovsky et al. [ImageNet Large Scale Visual Recognition Challenge](https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.0575). International Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV), 115(3):211-252, 2015."""@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "image-classification-tf-dicom" ;
    dcterms:license <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/licence/APACHE_2_0> ;
    dcterms:modified "2025-08-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:title "Chest x-ray image classifier"@en ;
    dcterms:type <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/category/AI4_inference>,
        <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/category/AI4_pre_trained>,
        <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/category/AI4_trainable> ;
    dcat:keyword "deep learning"@en .

<https://api.cloud.ai4eosc.eu/v1/catalog/modules/integrated-plant-protection/metadata> a it6:MachineLearningModel ;
    it6:hasMachineLearningLibrary <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/library/PyTorch> ;
    it6:hasRepository <https://github.com/ai4os-hub/integrated-plant-protection>,
        <https://hub.docker.com/r/ai4oshub/integrated-plant-protection> ;
    it6:hasTaskType <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/tasktype/Classification>,
        <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/tasktype/Computer_Vision> ;
    it6:shortDescription "A Torch model to classify plants."@en ;
    it6:trainedOn <https://zenodo.org/records/15873360> ;
    dcterms:created "2024-07-03"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:description """The module contains 2 fine-tuned models.
Fine-tunning pipeline is implemented in [PyTorch](https://pytorch.org/).
Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN) serve as the backbone architecture for classifiers.

For rye images, pretrained `ResNet-34` model was used and named `rye-34`.
For beet images, pretrained `ResNet-101` model was used and named `beet-101`.

Images are preprocessed with normalization and resizing to 256x256 before being fed to the models.
For data augmentation, training images are randomly cropped and flipped horizontally.
The output layer of each classifier is adjusted to the number of classes
We have `brown_rust`,`uneffected` classes for rye and `cercospora`,`uneffected` classes for beet.
Result of the model consists of tensor of shape (batch_size, num_classes) containing the predicted classes logits.
The API returns the predicted class with the highest logit value for each input image along with the corresponding probability of the predicted class.


Cross-entropy loss is the objective function used to guide model training in classification tasks
An SGD optimizer with momentum is used to update the model weights.
A learning rate scheduler reduces the learning rate by a factor of 0.1 every 7 epochs.
The training process lasts for 20 epochs per model."""@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "integrated-plant-protection" ;
    dcterms:license <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/licence/APACHE_2_0> ;
    dcterms:modified "2025-07-25"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:title "Integrated Plant Protection"@en ;
    dcterms:type <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/category/AI4_inference>,
        <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/category/AI4_pre_trained> ;
    dcat:keyword "deep learning"@en,
        "image classification"@en .

<https://api.cloud.ai4eosc.eu/v1/catalog/modules/litter-assessment/metadata> a it6:MachineLearningModel ;
    it6:hasMachineLearningLibrary <http://w3id.org/ai4os/vocabulary/library/TensorFlow> ;
